 It operates through Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (APIs) and Formulations segments. The company provides fermentation based active pharmaceutical ingredients in immunosuppressants, anti-bacterial, oncology, antifungal, and other therapeutic areas. It also offers tacrolimus, mycophenolate mofetil, mycophenolate sodium, cyclosporine, sirolimus, voclosporin, and pimecrolimus for immunosuppressants therapeutic segment; and temsirolimus, everolimus, romidepsin, doxorubicin, mitomycin, midostaurin, and dactinomycin for oncology therapeutic segment. In addition, the company provides mupirocin, mupirocin calcium, polymyxin B sulfate, fidaxomicin, vancomycin hydrochloride, daptomycin, fusidic acid, colistimethate sodium, and teicoplanin for anti-bacterial applications; anidulafungin, caspofungi acetate, micafungin sodium, and nystatin for anti-fungal therapeutic segment; and lovastatin and pravastatin sodium for other applications. Further, the company provides contract research and manufacturing services in the areas of fermentation and semi-synthesis products. Concord Biotech Limited was incorporated in 1984 and is based in Ahmedabad, India.","beta":0.441,"sharesOutstanding":209232408,"marketCap":114952298496,"trailingPE":41.5897,"forwardPE":26.5737,"priceToBook":5.6241,"enterpriseToEbitda":27.133,"dividendYield":0.69,"heldPercentInsiders":0.7249,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.1496,"earningsGrowth":0.103,"revenueGrowth":0.251,"website":"https://www.concordbiotech.com","fullTimeEmployees":1624,"recommendationKey":"none","targetMeanPrice":760.5,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":5,"financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":{"0q":{"avg":null,"low":null,"high":null,"yearAgoEps":null,"numberOfAnalysts":null,"growth":null,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1q":{"avg":null,"low":null,"high":null,"yearAgoEps":null,"numberOfAnalysts":null,"growth":null,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"0y":{"avg":15.8707,"low":15.15,"high":16.9,"yearAgoEps":12.507,"numberOfAnaly